# Edited Excerpts from a Smithsonian Seminar Series--Part 3: The Humanities and Social Sciences.

**Authors:** Borden, Carla M., Ed., And Others

## Abstract
The third article in a series of excerpts from seminars sponsored by the Smithsonian Institution on knowledge collaboration focuses on the humanities and social sciences. Reasons for the relatively greater frequency of collaborative research in the natural sciences are examined, and examples of collaborative projects in the humanities and social sciences are described. (10 references) (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ451797

